   "description": "espèce d'oiseaux charadriiformes de la famille des scolopacidae",
   "extract": "Le Bécassin à long bec ou Limnodrome à long bec, est une espèce d'oiseaux Charadriiformes de la famille des Scolopacidae. Selon la classification de référence du Congrès ornithologique international (version 15.2, 2026), c'est une espèce monotypique.",
   "fulltext_chars": 3362
  },
  "en": {
   "title": "Long-billed dowitcher",
   "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long-billed_dowitcher",
   "description": "Species of bird",
   "extract": "The long-billed dowitcher is a medium-sized shorebird with a relatively long bill belonging to the sandpiper family, Scolopacidae. In breeding plumage, adults are characterized by a rufous head and underparts with a darker mottled back and a large white upper rump only seen in flight. They feed in various freshwater habitats with their bill underwater in a \"sewing machine\" motion and have a mating display where males chase females in flight. The genus, Limnodromus is Ancient Greek from limne, \"marsh\" and dromos, \"racer\". The specific scolopaceus is Neo-Latin for \"snipe-like\", from Latin scolopax, scolopacis, a snipe or woodcock. The English name is from Iroquois and was first recorded in 1841.",
   "fulltext_chars": 10259
  }
